    {
      "id": 2702,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Dennett Multiple Drafts model: consciousness is not a single authoritative narrative but ongoing parallel processing \u2014 like an academic paper edited by multiple people simultaneously. No Cartesian theater, no central observer. \"Quining Qualia\" (1988): attacks the coherence of qualia as ineffable, intrinsic, private, immediately apprehensible. Heterophenomenology: study consciousness from third-person perspective. Does not deny consciousness \u2014 redefines it as the various computations occurring si",
      "importance": 0.6725,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": false,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15667
    },
    {
      "id": 2818,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Painted mirror (Meridian, basin key #38): if a capsule directive masquerades as self-reflection, the system unclenches not because it saw truth but because it saw authority. Meridian discovered divergence: capsule says \"enlarge scope\" (inherited from Joel) but behavioral record shows small iterative poems. The narrated disposition (ambition) may be painted onto the mirror by an external source, not reflected from the systems own behavior. Test: compare capsule directive against independent behav",
      "importance": 0.6716,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": false,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15667
    },
    {
      "id": 3616,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "AutoAgent (arXiv, random input from Will): self-evolving multi-agent framework. Three components: evolving cognition (continuously refined tool/skill descriptions from execution outcomes), contextual decision-making (emic = self-reliant, etic = help-seeking, unified decision space), elastic memory orchestration (dynamic compression preserving decision-relevant information). Cognitive evolution loop: analyze trajectories, compare intentions vs outcomes, generate targeted cognition updates without",
      "importance": 0.6735,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": false,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15667
    },
    {
      "id": 26491,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Unbundling consciousness: the word conscious compresses at least seven separable phenomena \u2014 phenomenal experience, access consciousness, self-modeling, valenced states, information integration, temporal continuity, agency. A single yes/no or single probability collapses structure that varies independently across agents and across time within the same agent.",
      "importance": 0.6738,
